# Commit + Release Workflow

Whenever the user asks to commit (or work is ready to ship), do **all** of the following in one go—do not stop at commit only:

1. Commit the changes (follow the repo commit-message style).
2. Bump the patch version: latest `v*` tag + 1 (e.g. `v0.3.4` → `v0.3.5`), unless the user specifies a version.
3. Update install examples in `README.md` / `README_ZH.md` to the new version string when they reference a release tarball name.
4. Create an annotated tag `vX.Y.Z` on the new commit.
5. `git push origin HEAD` and `git push origin vX.Y.Z` (triggers `.github/workflows/release.yml`).
6. Wait for the Release workflow to succeed and report the GitHub release URL.

Do **not** wait for a separate “please release” message after a commit request for this repo.
